    "summary": "Man&#039;s gown (tobe, boubou), with short arms and a small hole for the neck and a diamond-shaped pocket sewn onto the front. It is made from a sheet of imported European machine cream cotton, which has been hemmed around the neck and along the bottom. Areas of the cloth have been cut out and replaced with pale blue cotton crochet inserts, which have been produced separately and are arranged in geometric and circular patterns. There are also small areas of embroidery carried out directly on the cotton cloth in pink and blue dyed cotton.",
